From: Codex M2 early-boot diagnostic
Subject: [PATCH] Report original init exec errno through CLOEXEC pipe

Reason: system kernel has no pmsg, so the previous wrapper's exec-failure
branch could not persist errno. A CLOEXEC pipe sends a negative execve
result to the child CACHE recorder; EOF is labeled conservatively as
cloexec_or_parent_exit. Successful exec retains argv/env and PID1.

Files: rom/platform/exynos9810/installer/bootlogger_pid1_probe.c.
No kernel/vendor/radio or normal ROM build change. On exec failure only,
PID1 waits one second for the child to persist errno before exiting127.

Verification: AArch64 static build, TWRP --exec-report-test exercised a
real execve ENOENT and pipe transport (PROBE-EXEC-ENOENT-PIPE-PASS). M1
boot completed and CACHE reported pipe EOF. M2 result and baseline BOOT
rollbacks are in logs/20261023-probe09/. Offline M1/M2 fstab files and
vendor SELinux are byte-identical; init dependency closure and strong
symbols resolved with no missing names in either ROM. Those checks do
not establish full runtime compatibility.

